@dbuniversity{Bocher.2018,
 abstract = {Train stations as well as cinema are places of mobility. Trains and movies transfer people to different places and open up new perspectives. In this sense the cinema screen can be compared to a window of a moving train. Movies, traveling and transportation mirrors the way we see the world and change it in the process. The city of Los Angeles can be seen as the central station of movie making in the world, which at the same time features Union Station as the last great transportation center. We chose Los Angeles' Union Station because it is not only the last Grand Station of America, but also one of the most filmed train station in the world. In this paper we explore the connection between Union Station as a motion picture star and a transportation hub for the Western US. More specifically we interrogate how and why Union Station is an ongoing film location for Hollywood. To accomplish our goal, we acquired data from Film L.A. That documented film occurrences in Los Angeles from 2008 to},
